<http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#TargetCommunity> <http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#promptExtractionText> "Extract Target Community elements from the image. Target Community includes: audience indicators, community markers, demographic cues, cultural references, community-specific elements, and target audience signals. For each community element found, provide: 1) A descriptive instance_name (e.g., 'internet_audience', 'meme_culture'), 2) A natural language label (e.g., 'the internet audience', 'the meme culture'), 3) A brief description of the intended audience or community. Focus on elements that indicate who the meme is designed for. Example output format: {\"instance_name\": \"internet_audience\", \"label\": \"the internet audience\", \"description\": \"The meme appears designed for internet-savvy audiences familiar with meme culture and dark humor\"}"@en .
_:n8dbceb68725c4eddab6f8ad5ae353c35b21 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#first> <http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#VisualMaterial> .
