<http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01329#audience_id> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The target audience for this meme is individuals familiar with and appreciative of edgy humor and internet meme culture, particularly those who understand and find comedic value in the juxtaposition of romanticized cowboy imagery with vulgar, confrontational language. The meme appeals to a demographic that enjoys shock value and irony, often found in online communities that engage with subversive or provocative content. The cultural reference to Western American cowboy stereotypes is leveraged to create humor, suggesting the audience is likely to recognize and appreciate this specific cultural trope. The use of explicit language ('motherfuckers') indicates the meme is intended for an audience comfortable with offensive or taboo humor, which is a common characteristic of edgy humor communities. The visual elements (cowboy hats, guns, lasso) and the text ('it's time to play cowboys') are designed to resonate with viewers who are familiar with the cowboy archetype and its associated tropes, making the meme most effective for those who can interpret the irony and the subversion of the wholesome cowboy image."@en .
<http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#VisualCompositionCompliant> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Visual Composition Compliant"@en .
_:n8dbceb68725c4eddab6f8ad5ae353c35b101 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#first> <http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#TextualMaterial> .
<http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#Object-embedded> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#VisualWorldPart> .
<http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#ContextualExpansion> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01329#vulgar_language_use> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The text 'saddle up motherfuckers' and 'it's time to play cowboys' employs explicit, offensive language ('motherfuckers') to subvert the wholesome or romanticized image of cowboys. This linguistic choice is a key part of the meme's humor or shock value, relying on the contrast between the visual cowboy imagery and the crude, confrontational tone of the text. Understanding the impact of this language requires knowledge of its social and cultural connotations outside the image."@en .
<http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#motionBlurIntegratedWith> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> _:n8dbceb68725c4eddab6f8ad5ae353c35b52 .
