<http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01329#edgy_humor> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The meme relies on 'edgy humor' — a comedic style that uses shock value, taboo language, or controversial imagery to provoke laughter or attention. This requires background knowledge of internet meme culture and the conventions of edgy humor, which often juxtapose offensive or extreme content with mundane or wholesome visuals to create a comedic effect. The combination of cowboy imagery with vulgar language is a classic example of this."@en .
<http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#opaqueOverlaidOn> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#diegeticallyIntegratedWith> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subPropertyOf> <http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#relatesTo> .
<http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#verticallyAdjacentTo> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subPropertyOf> <http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#geometricallyAdjacentTo> .
<http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#visualWorldPartOf> <http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#relationIndex> "46"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> .
_:n8dbceb68725c4eddab6f8ad5ae353c35b65 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#rest> _:n8dbceb68725c4eddab6f8ad5ae353c35b66 .
<http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01329#semiotic_projection_1> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The user is implicitly projected onto the scene 'cowboys_ready_for_action' as someone who is being called to join or participate in the confrontational 'cowboy' activity. The text 'saddle up motherfuckers' and 'it's time to play cowboys' functions as a direct address or invitation to the viewer, creating a sense of inclusion or participation in the depicted scenario. The user is not explicitly addressed with 'you' or 'me', but the imperative tone and the call to action strongly imply that the viewer is the intended recipient of the command, making the scene a projection of the user's potential role or identity within the meme's narrative."@en .
_:n8dbceb68725c4eddab6f8ad5ae353c35b82 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
